1) STATIC — signatures: read=FsReadCap, write=FsWriteCap, no FsRead on write
========================================================================

### ooda/std/os/fs.oo (product-aligned sealed names)

```
pub fn fs_write_file(fs: &FsWriteCap, ...)  → write_file(fs, ...)
pub fn fs_read_file(fs: &FsReadCap, ...)    → read_file(fs, ...)
pub fn fs_path_exists(fs: &FsReadCap, ...)  → path_exists(fs, ...)
pub fn fs_file_size(fs: &FsReadCap, ...)    → file_size(fs, ...)
```

Static grep prove:
```
OK no FsReadCap on write signatures
OK reads use FsReadCap
```

### std/src/fs.oo (repo std facade)

```
pub fn fs_write_file(fs: &FsWriteCap, ...)  → fs_write(fs, ...)
pub fn fs_read_file(fs: &FsReadCap, ...)    → fs_read(fs, ...)
```

**Claim 1+2 (sig):** PASS — write params are FsWriteCap only; read params are FsReadCap only.
**Claim 3 (sig):** PASS — no write function takes `&FsReadCap`.

========================================================================
2) STATIC — sealed map + runtime (CAP-G2 contract that CAP-G6 threads into)
========================================================================

### check: sealed_fs_kind_of (`oodac/check_cap_util.oo`)

| Sealed name | Preferred kind |
|-------------|----------------|
| `read_file` | **FsReadCap** |
| `fs_read` | **FsReadCap** |
| `path_exists` | **FsReadCap** |
| `file_size` | **FsReadCap** |
| `write_file` | **FsWriteCap** |
| `fs_write` | **FsWriteCap** |

Helpers: `cap_fs_granted_ok` / `cap_fs_argflow_ok` accept **exact preferred OR legacy FsCap**.
**No inverted bag:** FsReadCap does not authorize write; FsWriteCap does not authorize read.

### runtime (`chs_rt_fs.c` + `chs_rt_sys.c`)

| Op | Require | Accepts |
|----|---------|---------|
| `oo_read_file` | `oo_cap_require_fsread` | `g_tok_fsread` **or** `g_tok_fs` |
| `oo_write_file` | `oo_cap_require_fswrite` | `g_tok_fswrite` **or** `g_tok_fs` |
| path_exists / file_size | `oo_cap_require_fsread` | same as read |

Wrong granular (`g_tok_fsread` on write / `g_tok_fswrite` on read) → `ERR\tcap\t…` + exit 1.
Write still gated by `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` after require (policy overlay; not a Cap type).

**Claim 1+2 (map/runtime):** PASS.
**Claim 3 (runtime):** PASS — write path never calls `require_fsread`.

