### Alias free-names `fs_read` / `fs_write` (honesty residual)

| Call | Cap wrong | Check result | Cap correct |
|------|-----------|--------------|-------------|
| `fs_write` + FsReadCap | **DENY** prefer FsWriteCap | sealed map live | type: `undefined variable 'fs_write'` (not in `tc_names`) |
| `fs_read` + FsWriteCap | **DENY** prefer FsReadCap | sealed map live | type: `undefined variable 'fs_read'` |

**Interpretation:** sealed **cap map** includes alias names (`fs_read`/`fs_write`) for
fail-closed preferred kinds, but product free builtins registered in `tc_names.oo`
are **`read_file` / `write_file` only**. ooda thin wrappers correctly call product
names. **std/src/fs.oo residual:** bodies call `fs_read`/`fs_write` (alias names) —
signature migration PASS; body names are honesty residual (prefer `read_file`/
`write_file` like ooda/std/os/fs.oo, or register aliases in tc/emit). **Not** a
FsRead-on-write hole: wrong-cap still DENY via sealed map; correct-cap type-fails
rather than fail-open.

